


##  Phase 1: Environment & Architecture
- [ ] **Dockerization**
    - [ ] Create `Dockerfile` for Backend (Go).
    - [ ] Create `Dockerfile` for Frontend (Next.js/Vue/Svelte).
    - [ ] Setup `docker-compose.yml` to link both containers.
- [X] **Database Setup**
    - [X] Initialize SQLite database.
    - [X] Setup `golang-migrate`.
    - [X] Create first migration: `000001_create_users_table`.
- [X] **Backend Skeleton**
    - [X] Setup Clean Architecture folders (`cmd`, `internal/repo`, `internal/service`, `internal/handler`).
    - [X] Implement `Config` loader and `Logger`.
    - [X] Implement `CORS` and `Rate Limiter` middleware.

##  Phase 2: Authentication & User Management
- [X] **Database Schema**
    - [X] `users` table (Email, PW, Name, DOB, Avatar, Nickname, AboutMe, PrivacyStatus).
    - [X] `sessions` table (UUID, UserID, ExpiresAt).
- [ ] **Backend Logic**
    - [X] Registration (Bcrypt password hashing).
    - [X] Login (Session creation + Cookie setting).
    - [X] Logout (Cookie clearing + Session deletion).
    - [X] Middleware: `RequireAuth` (Validate session from cookie).
- [ ] **Frontend Logic**
    - [X] Register/Login forms with validation.
    - [X] Persistent login state (Check session on load).

## Phase 3: Profile & Followers
- [X] **Database Schema**
    - [X] `followers` table (FollowerID, FollowingID, Status: 'pending'/'accepted').
- [X] **Features**
    - [X] Toggle Profile Privacy (Public vs Private).
    - [X] Follow/Unfollow logic:
        - [ ] If Public: Auto-accept.
        - [ ] If Private: Send request (Notification).
    - [X] Profile Page: Show User Info + Activity + Followers/Following lists.

##  Phase 4: Posts & Comments
- [X] **Database Schema**
    - [X] `posts` table (AuthorID, Content, ImagePath, Privacy: 'public'/'almost_private'/'private').
    - [X] `post_allowed_users` (For 'private' posts to specific followers).
    - [X] `comments` table.
- [X] **Features**
    - [X] Create Post (Support JPEG, PNG, GIF).
    - [X] Create Comment.
    - [X] Post Visibility Filter:
        - [X] Public: Everyone.
        - [X] Almost Private: Followers only.
        - [X] Private: Only specific chosen followers.

##  Phase 5: Groups & Events
- [ ] **Database Schema**
    - [ ] `groups` table (CreatorID, Title, Description).
    - [ ] `group_members` table.
    - [ ] `group_events` table (Title, Description, DateTime).
    - [ ] `event_votes` table (Going / Not Going).
- [ ] **Features**
    - [ ] Create Group / Browse Groups.
    - [ ] Join Request (Only creator accepts).
    - [ ] Group Invitations (Members can invite others).
    - [ ] Group Posts & Comments (Visible to members only).
    - [ ] Event Creation & "Going/Not Going" voting.

## Real-time Chat (WebSockets)
- [ ] **Backend WebSocket Hub**
    - [ ] Handle connections/disconnections.
    - [ ] Map `UserID` to `websocket.Conn`.
- [ ] **Private Chat**
    - [ ] Logic: Only if one follows the other.
    - [ ] Emoji support.
- [ ] **Group Chat**
    - [ ] Common room for all group members.
- [ ] **Real-time Status**
    - [ ] (Optional but good) Show who is online/offline.

##  Phase 7: Notification System
- [ ] **Features**
    - [ ] Notify on Follow Request.
    - [ ] Notify on Group Invitation.
    - [ ] Notify on Group Join Request (for creator).
    - [ ] Notify on New Group Event.
- [ ] **UI**
    - [ ] Notification bell visible on every page.
    - [ ] Separate UI from private messages.

##  Phase 8: Image Handling
- [ ] **Backend Logic**
    - [ ] Image upload handler (Validation: JPEG, PNG, GIF).
    - [ ] File system storage (save path in DB).
    - [ ] Static file server (to serve uploaded images).

